{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01005",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.56,
      "end_seconds": 6.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.97,
      "end_seconds": 11.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.31,
      "end_seconds": 20.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "I've been feeling cold all the time, and I wanted to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.01,
      "end_seconds": 27.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Okay, did it come on recently? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.34,
      "end_seconds": 34.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Probably two years. Yeah. And tiredness, too. I've been putting on weight too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.05,
      "end_seconds": 38.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Any heavy periods, trouble swallowing or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.75,
      "end_seconds": 43.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Actually, no, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.78,
      "end_seconds": 49.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Have you had any hair loss or swelling in the neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.21,
      "end_seconds": 53.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.36,
      "end_seconds": 58.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Right, is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.1,
      "end_seconds": 63.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Right, no problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.87,
      "end_seconds": 67.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Right, have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.67,
      "end_seconds": 80.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.9,
      "text": "I had a mole taken off my arm a few years ago. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.07,
      "end_seconds": 89.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.34,
      "end_seconds": 93.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "It's iron tablets, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.98,
      "end_seconds": 98.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.94,
      "end_seconds": 106.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "My brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.23,
      "end_seconds": 122.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.55,
      "end_seconds": 135.19,
      "duration_seconds": 10.64,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.77,
      "end_seconds": 146.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.44,
      "end_seconds": 151.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I have low haemoglobin, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.16,
      "end_seconds": 157.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "I follow. Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.63,
      "end_seconds": 162.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Mm, no allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.97,
      "end_seconds": 165.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.24,
      "end_seconds": 180.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.04,
      "end_seconds": 209.09,
      "duration_seconds": 10.05,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 67, height 163 centimetres, BP is 126 over 72, temp 36.7 degrees, weight 63 kilos, BMI works out to 23.7."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.07,
      "end_seconds": 211.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.68,
      "end_seconds": 216.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.57,
      "end_seconds": 222.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.43,
      "end_seconds": 225.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.27,
      "end_seconds": 248.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Your pulse is slow, about fifty-six, and the thyroid isn't enlarged."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.0,
      "end_seconds": 253.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.05,
      "end_seconds": 267.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Reflexes are a bit slow to relax."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.17,
      "end_seconds": 275.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.26,
      "end_seconds": 317.22,
      "duration_seconds": 26.96,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, my working impression is an underactive thyroid. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'd also keep depression in mind. Let's book a thyroid test to look into hypothyroid symptoms. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's book blood tests to look into fatigue."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.9,
      "end_seconds": 320.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.11,
      "end_seconds": 351.13,
      "duration_seconds": 30.02,
      "text": "The treatment will be levothyroxine, 50 micrograms, every morning on an empty stomach, until we review. It's for hypothyroidism. Take the thyroid tablet on an empty stomach, half an hour before breakfast, and not with calcium or iron. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.84,
      "end_seconds": 354.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Okay, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.77,
      "end_seconds": 365.22,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.82,
      "end_seconds": 369.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}